    "night": 5,
    "resident": "dalia",
    "truth": "human",
    "anomalies": [],
    "title": "The reference person",
    "opening": "Kest has removed the department title from her badge. The glue has left a rectangle paler than the rest of the plastic.",
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "where",
        "q": "Where have you been?",
        "a": "The containment laboratory. I was asked to calibrate against a photograph of somebody who had not yet been detained. That should have been impossible. It was merely efficient.",
        "mood": "guarded"
      },
      {
        "id": "home",
        "q": "Who is waiting for you upstairs?",
        "a": "Lives alone; research colleague: Selene Holt. A measurement can be accurate and the question it answers can still be wrong.",
        "mood": "neutral"
      },
      {
        "id": "detail",
        "q": "Does the system create Reproductions?",
        "a": "It does not create them from nothing. The rain leaves a capacity to repeat. The census gives it names, addresses and corrections. We thought we were detecting a difference. Sometimes we were teaching the difference to disappear.",
        "mood": "uneasy"
      },
      {
        "id": "follow",
        "q": "Does that make every Echo dangerous?",
        "a": "No. It makes our confidence dangerous. Some returns have lived quietly for years. Some learn only how to open doors. You need conduct, witnesses and history. None is perfect. Together they are better than my meter.",
        "requires": [
          "detail"
        ],
        "mood": "guarded"
      },
      {
        "id": "gentle",
        "q": "Take a breath. What do you need me to understand?",
        "a": "I need you to know I understood too late. That is not an excuse. It is simply the part I can no longer edit.",
        "tone": "gentle",
        "group": "approach",
        "mood": "open"
      },
      {
        "id": "press",
        "q": "I need an explanation, not a rehearsed answer.",
        "a": "The visitor looks at the recorder before answering. “Then turn that off before you ask me to trust you.”",
        "tone": "press",
        "group": "approach",
        "mood": "defensive"
      }
    ],
    "archive": "Lab protocol describes reference photographs applied BEFORE containment. The revision date predates the official discovery of Reproductions.",
    "call": "Anja: “Kest asked me which circuit feeds the loudspeakers. She explicitly told me not to touch ventilation. She is trying to stop something, not shut us down.”",
    "hold": "A second paper arrives from the outer desk. Lab protocol describes reference photographs applied BEFORE containment. The revision date predates the official discovery of Reproductions.",
    "disposition": "ordinary",
    "event": "",
    "evidence": "protocol",
    "evidenceLabel": "Pre-containment reference protocol",
    "evidenceText": "The programme applies identity references before detaining people. The census can shape the phenomenon it claims only to detect.",
